nerable settings safe so  our long-term care settings retirement  homes hospital sectors and other  congregate settings  and once we can maintain that safe  supply to ensure that patients are  protected  in those settings we will move down our  framework and provide them to be more  accessible and available and i'm sorry  the global supply is so limited but  we're your government is working  diligently to provide increased  availability of these tests  next question  yes hello so i just i was just wondering  dr moore if you could comment in french  about what you were saying about the  administration of third doses in the  education sector  um  with your permission stella i i continue  to take my french lessons and i don't  think i'm  fluent enough at present  but  our third dose strategy for workers is  to try to ensure that we can increase  the access for all child care workers  all staff  in education settings to be able to have  access for their third doses we're  working with school boards  with third parties that can provide  the immunization support we know our  health system partners our hospitals our  public health units are  fully active trying to immunize the  general population following our  guidelines so we're trying to provide  this additional resource to increase  access for staff in those settings to  get their third dose we're aiming to  have them up and running as you've heard  from the education announcement uh as  soon as possible um to provide uh the  level of protection um uh as we  further open our school settings um so  it's uh  all uh  aspects of the health system are working  diligently to try to protect uh the  staff in those environments  yes i had another question about rapid  tests  i was wondering what would you say to  someone who looks for example to do  who's trying to find  some rapid tests and see that there will  no longer be  some pop-up clinics uh on january 14 and  what do you say to to them so to people  who want to procure 