ination turning five um today you'd  be eligible uh for your vaccination uh  and i'm sorry the booking system uh  is getting fixed to ensure that we have  a you can't book if you're four  and haven't turned five so um that that  would be fixed in the coming days uh but  just so individuals won't go to  immunization clinic expecting to be  immunized if you're not five they  for the most part  unless there's a off-label decision by a  health care provider will not receive  the vaccine  follow-up and this is the last question  great yeah so you had mentioned that  there is a plan in place to return to  school january 17th um there's a number  of things that you mentioned have been  done like um more filters and and 95s  for staff things like that uh is it  realistic though to expect children will  be back in class given the explosion in  case numbers anything more you can you  can share is that a realistic timeline  well the the opening of schools  certainly is a decision of government i  i think we all understand that there's  negatives and positives to keeping our  schools closed uh and i i like all of my  colleagues in public health uh hope uh  that we can have our children back in  for in-person learning as soon as  possible so in the interim  despite that aspirational goal and with  that aspirational goal we are  further immunizing first second and  third doses for the staff of child care  and in education  we are further providing first and  second doses to children five to eleven  we're further purchasing additional  n95  and high grade mass for children where  three thousand additional hepa filters  have been purchased and we're  interested in putting those in in play  as soon as possible  and we're viewing all of our guidelines  uh to ensure we're keeping up  to  the standard on protecting our schools  as well as reviewing all environmental  health cleaning and ventilation  standards so that works getting done um  we're working in the background  i think all s